Hi,

The softmax function in transformers is applied over the query-key dot product space to help the transformer selectively attend to different positions in a sequence. In other words, its function is to transform the dot products into probabilities, which indicate the “importance” (probability) of each position for a given target sequence position.

In this way, the softmax function allows the transformer to distribute the ‘attention weights’ among the positions, with the adaptive nature of these weights allowing the model to learn the optimal attention regions.

On the other hand, the mask matrix in multihead attention is used to preclude (or mask) positions that we do not wish the model to consider during training (generally for target states where we are predicting future states).

By multiplying the mask matrix with the attention scores, we effectively eliminates any sequence as a prediction target for a sequence by setting the attention scores to negative infinity. As a result, these masked entries do not contribute to the subsequent calculation of weighted sums in the self-attention block.

I hope this helps you understand the usage and significance of both softmax and mask matrix in Transformer models.

Best wishes,

