The role of the softmax function closely follows the standard implementation of a fully connected layer. The difference here is that the softmax function is applied to the attention-scores instead of a standard feature space.

In a neural network, the role of a softmax is to calculate the probabilities over output categories so that they add up to 1.0. This is not the only way to apply a softmax layer. Rather, it can be applied anywhere in the network wherever the concept of probabilities is needed.

Similarly, in Transformers, the softmax function is used to assign probabilities over the input sequence for predicting a specific position in the sequence. After the query and key vectors are dotted together and transformed, the softmax layer is applied to assign the probabilities. These probabilities give us a score for attending to every element in the other sequence for the generation of the attention-vectors.

So, the softmax function in Transformers plays a similar role as in a normal neural network. Its function is to make the output a probability distribution.

