## Continuous Learning:

We have to understand what learning a model is before understanding continuous learning. When the machine learning model is trained, that means the model is learning in order to perform its best to infer on the unseen data.

When a model is performing good after training it for a certain batch then we can save that model which has learned from all those batches and then we can resume the learning on the new batches to further improve the model performance. This is called **Continuous Learning**.

When we have a trained model which is performing well then who would resist not to take advantage of the trained model? If there is an incoming batch of data, let's say containing a feature which was not previously available in training, we can resume the training of the model with previous knowledge, i.e. weights, and learn the current incoming data batch with new feature available with it.

