Logprob shows the probabilities computed by the model i.e. negative log loss value of the top prediction. It also includes the probabilities of other predictions to help you debug your predictions.

What is the '--word-margin=' argument used for in profile.sh?

This argument is used to passing word margin value while training the model. Word margin value is used in models that have segmental conditioning, indicating the change in likelihood of the model's output due to a specific word boundary. This value helps the model distinguish the annotations from the phonemes. This argument is not used in the training of non-segmental conditioning models like DNN-HMM.
[180/200] Running: How to measure and reduce TTFT on Gaudi?...

🧠 LLM Response:


TTFT is Time To First Tower (from top of peak to bottom of valley of histogram), using TTR (Time To Run) as axis. It is directly related on how long it takes for events to be generated in full (TTTR) (TTTR ~ TTFT).

